Amazon.com XXXX XXXX : XXXX I returned my order to Amazon via the XXXX XXXX label they provided to me. I dropped off the package at the XXXX store, and the XXXX driver listed my return package. During this time, I have been contacting Amazon every week about the issue that the package is missing, but they never took any action. I then reached out to XXXX. According to the XXXX agent, they have a contract with Amazon, and every time there is a listed package, Amazon is the one who should report it to XXXX and receive the reimbursement from UPS. 

According to XXXX, they have already issued a refund or reimbursement check to Amazon for the lost package. However, Amazon refused to issue my refund, so the product that they reimbursed is now lost. In the end, Amazon agreed to issue my refund, but due to a system issue, I am unable to get the money. Amazon has refused to help me since then. Fortunately, I have all the evidence, including emails and screenshots, to prove my case. 

The missing package is XXXX XXXX, amount in ORDER PLACED XX/XX/2023, Grand Total : {$2500.00}

On XX/XX/XXXX I received several emails from XXXX confirming transactions for hotels in NJ that I had just booked. Upon receiving these, and being that I am in Iowa and have no intention of going to NJ, I knew that these were fraudulent. So i immediately ( that night within minutes ) contacted XXXX and alerted them. In the ensuing XXXX hours of being transferred around they refused to help me and told that because these were booked through there " sister-site '' booking.com, even though the confirmations came from XXXX and the person who made broke into my XXXX account XXXX that they could not help me. They would then transfer me to booking.com who would then refuse to help and transfer me back to XXXX, this went on for a couple hours. After getting no-where and basically in tears at this point I gave and called my credit card company Chase. They assured me that their fraud department would take care of the pending charges on my account and that would only need to wait till morning to contact them. So the next day I called and filled out the required paperwork and trusted them to take it from there. Two months later I received a follow up phone call stating that since they couldn't verify that my account had been hacked they were sustaining the charges and I would have to pay them. 

I pointed that I had called while the charges were still pending and asked why they paid them at all, to which they said that " I just didn't know how it worked '' and that pending charges have to be paid to " certain vendors like XXXX ''. I asked why if XXXX had canceled XXXX of the charges the first night for fraud, which they did, why wouldn't all be treated that way and I was told that was between me and XXXX and they wouldn't do anything to help me. I was then told that all of this would noted on my account but that if I wanted to further dispute this I would have to contact XXXX. Which I did. After spending another hour and change on the phone XXXX agreed that another XXXX of them was fraud and instructed me to have Chase call them back for a refund, so i contacted Chase again and they refused to help me any further so i canceled the card. 

The charges appeared on my bill as follows : All appear on XX/XX/XXXX, in the amounts of {$170.00} {$160.00} {$140.00} {$170.00} {$170.00} {$170.00}
